;; Conformance fixture: data-classification/frame-http-carrier-extends-defaults
;;
;; Per Spec 015 §Tests (the `frame-http-carrier-extends-defaults.edn` row),
;; Spec 014 §Privacy, and EP-0015 §3 — a frame-local
;; `:sensitive {:http {:headers ["X-Honeycomb-Team"]}}` carrier name redacts
;; that header IN ADDITION TO the immutable built-in defaults (`Authorization`,
;; `Cookie`, `X-API-Key`, …); no frame can REMOVE a built-in default. App-
;; specific carriers are frame policy — the frame extension set UNIONS onto
;; the framework defaults, it never replaces them.
;;
;; Mode-B pure-call (`:redact-headers`): the HTTP header carrier denylist is a
;; leaf fn (`re-frame.http.privacy-headers/redact-headers`) — a pure
;; `(headers-map, frame-extras) → redacted-map` projection. `:frame-extras`
;; is the lower-cased carrier extension set the frame slice lowers a
;; `:sensitive {:http {:headers […]}}` declaration to. The fixture pins the
;; UNION semantics directly: a built-in default AND a frame carrier both
;; redact; an unclassified header rides verbatim.
;;
;; Two calls pin the union both ways: WITH the frame carrier (both redact)
;; and WITHOUT it (the built-in default STILL redacts — defaults are
;; unconditional; a frame cannot turn one off by omitting it).

{:fixture/id           :data-classification/frame-http-carrier-extends-defaults
 :fixture/spec-version "1.0"
 :fixture/capabilities #{:data-classification/classification-effects}
 :fixture/doc          "A frame-local :sensitive {:http {:headers [\"X-Honeycomb-Team\"]}} carrier redacts that header IN ADDITION to the immutable built-in HTTP header defaults (Authorization, …); the frame extension set UNIONS onto the defaults and no frame can remove a default. An unclassified header (Content-Type) rides verbatim (Spec 014 §Privacy / EP-0015 §3)."

 :fixture/calls
 [;; WITH the frame carrier extension: the built-in default Authorization AND
    ;; the frame carrier X-Honeycomb-Team both redact; Content-Type rides raw.
  {:call         :redact-headers
   :frame-extras #{"x-honeycomb-team"}
   :headers      {"Authorization"    "Bearer xyz"
                  "X-Honeycomb-Team" "team-key"
                  "Content-Type"     "application/json"}
   :expect       {"Authorization"    :rf/redacted
                  "X-Honeycomb-Team" :rf/redacted
                  "Content-Type"     "application/json"}}

  ;; WITHOUT the frame carrier: the built-in default STILL redacts
    ;; (defaults are unconditional), but the now-unclassified X-Honeycomb-Team
    ;; rides verbatim — proving the carrier extension, not the default, is
    ;; what redacted it in the first call.
  {:call         :redact-headers
   :headers      {"Authorization"    "Bearer xyz"
                  "X-Honeycomb-Team" "team-key"}
   :expect       {"Authorization"    :rf/redacted
                  "X-Honeycomb-Team" "team-key"}}]}
